{
  "name": "humanoid",
  "version": 2,
  "introduced_by": "shooter",
  "notes": "The root of everything that stands on two legs and carries something in its hands: a plain human figure in neutral greys, named by what each colour is for (body, limb, face, foot, eye, dark), so a child is a different person by its colours and its own ops. Drawn for the smooth bake at 18.5 mm voxels, 95 tall on a 40x96x40 grid: the trunk as one loft of elliptical slices, a voxel row each, along a hip, waist, chest and shoulder profile (stacked ellipsoids pinched into balloons where they met), limbs as tapering segments held a voxel or two clear of the trunk so an arm swings without tearing the chest (the upper arms and thighs are loose bones, closed surfaces of their own, so the hip and shoulder show no hole when they swing), flattened-ellipsoid feet, mitten hands with a thumb, and a head with a jaw, nose, ears and eyes. Eighteen bones, three to a limb, driven by src/anim/figure.rs from a body's movement rather than by an activity table. Nothing lists it in a biome; the bot and zombie classes are built on it.",
